# WP-267 review §4 ("Broke (lane, not linker)"): under --gc-sections c.o's
# new reference to __start_myreg/__stop_myreg revives u.o's `myreg`
# sections (a START_STOP root added by a changed file), so the output gains
# the section `myreg`, then loses it, then gains it again. The update falls
# back by name today; the dry run's oracle once counted every byte of a
# new output section as its tail (a lane defect, fixed by WP-267 P-4).
proves: a START_STOP root a changed file adds under --gc-sections revives an unchanged file's sections, and the oracle judges the new output section by its units and its tail
